<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Bead nexus-tko2w (RDR-108: document structure lives in the catalog manifest, never in chunk metadata).

    nexus.catalog_document_chunks gains three NULLABLE per-position labels and a marker:
        section_title TEXT, section_type TEXT, page_number INTEGER, labels_written BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false

    WHY. A T3 chunk row is content-addressed: one row per (tenant, collection, chash, model), and an
    upsert merges the metadata last-writer-wins (PgVectorRepository.mergeMetadata, jsonb concatenation).
    section_title, section_type and page_number are derived from a chunk's POSITION in one document, so
    when two documents hold the same chunk text one document's labels overwrite the other's on the shared
    row (RDR-232 research 7: ART RDR-084 position 24 carried RDR-002's title). The manifest row is already
    per (tenant, doc_id, position), so the labels belong there. The writers (CatalogRepository's single
    manifest insert), the manifest reads and chash_positions carry them; the search where-filter on these
    three keys is answered per (doc_id, position) from this table (PgVectorRepository label stage).

    LABELS_WRITTEN. NULL alone cannot say whether a row's label is "this document has no label here" or
    "this row was written before these columns existed". Reading both as the second would let a new
    document's unlabelled chunk inherit the shared chunk row's label, which belongs to whichever document
    wrote last. So the engine records, per manifest row, whether the writer sent the labels: true iff the
    incoming row carries any of the three label keys (a current client always sends all three, "" for a
    chunk with no heading) or says so with an explicit labels_written (a row read back and written again,
    as the re-embed move does). Old clients, the quarantine-restore reattach (plpgsql, vectors-025/030) and
    the manifest backfill send none and stay false. A reader trusts the manifest label of a true row (an
    empty one means "unlabelled") and falls back to the chunk row's own legacy label only for a false row.

    NO BACKFILL. Every existing row is false with NULL labels, which is the true prior state. The only
    source for a backfill is the shared T3 chunk row: exact for a chash with ONE live owner, the wrong
    value for a shared one. That single-owner backfill is a follow-up, not part of this change. A re-index
    of a document rewrites its manifest and fills the columns.

    ADD COLUMN only, four columns in ONE statement (no UPDATE, no ALTER ... TYPE ... USING), so there is no
    DATA EFFECT line, matching tuples-009-claimed-at.xml: scripts/data_effect_lint.py's own scope excludes
    ADD COLUMN. A nullable column with no default, and a NOT NULL column with a constant DEFAULT, are
    catalog-only changes in PostgreSQL 11 and later (no table rewrite). No new table, so no RLS, grant or
    jOOQ reflection-registration change. No index: the label filter is reached through the existing
    (tenant_id, chash) index and filtered per row.

    Placed after vectors-037-reembed-jobs.xml (the tail when this landed) and before the grants-nexus-svc.xml
    runAlways block (the established late-append convention, D0.1).
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="catalog-046-1" author="nexus-tko2w">
        <comment>Adds section_title TEXT, section_type TEXT and page_number INTEGER (all NULL) and labels_written BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false to nexus.catalog_document_chunks -- per-position labels, document-scoped by the manifest's (tenant_id, doc_id, position) key, and the marker that says whether a row's labels are its document's own answer. An additive ADD COLUMN only (no data mutation of any existing row), so no DATA EFFECT line applies per scripts/data_effect_lint.py's own scope. NULL labels with labels_written false is the true prior state of every existing row; a re-index fills them.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.catalog_document_chunks
    ADD COLUMN section_title  TEXT NULL,
    ADD COLUMN section_type   TEXT NULL,
    ADD COLUMN page_number    INTEGER NULL,
    ADD COLUMN labels_written BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true">
                ALTER TABLE nexus.catalog_document_chunks
                    DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS section_title,
                    DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS section_type,
                    DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS page_number,
                    DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS labels_written;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
